==English==

{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|NL.|en}} {{term|paraplegia|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|παραπληγία|tr=paraplēgia|lang=grc}}, Ionic Greek for {{term|παραπληξία||paralysis on one side|tr=paraplēksia|lang=grc}}, from {{term|παραπλήσσεσθαι||to be stricken on one side|tr=paraplēssesthai|lang=grc}}, active {{term|παραπλήσσειν||to strike on one side|tr=paraplēssein|lang=grc}}, from {{term|παρά||beside|tr=para|lang=grc}} + {{term|πλήσσειν||to strike|tr=plēssein|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{context|pathology|lang=en}} A [[condition]] where the lower half of a patient's body is [[paralyzed]] and cannot move.

====Related terms====
* [[monoplegia]]
* [[hemiplegia]]
* [[paraplegic]]
* [[quadriplegia]]

